{"ref":"BDB, שֹׁמְרוֹן","hw":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","html":"<big><span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁמְרוֹן</span></big><sub>109</sub>  <strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> capital of N. Isr. from Omri’s time <strong>(</strong><em>belonging to clan</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">שֶׁמֶר</span>, Sta<sup>ZAW v (1885), 165–175</sup>; originally <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמְרוֹן</span> or <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמְרַיִן</span>; Assyrian <em>Samerîna</em> COT <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:24\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.24\">1 K 16:24</a><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:24\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.24\">1 K 16:24</a> (name expl. as from <span dir=\"rtl\">שֶׁמֶר</span>, orig. owner of site), v <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:28\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.28\">28</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.29\">29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:32\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.32\">32</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 20:1\" href=\"/I_Kings.20.1\">20:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 20:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.20.10\">10</a> +; <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁמְר֫וֹנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 20:43\" href=\"/I_Kings.20.43\">1 K 20:43</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:19\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.19\">2 K 6:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 14:14\" href=\"/II_Kings.14.14\">14:14</a>; personified as woman <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:46\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.46\">Ez 16:46</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:51\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.51\">51</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:53\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.53\">53</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:55\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.55\">55</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.4\">23:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:33\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.33\">33</a>; king of N. Isarel is <span dir=\"rtl\">מֶלֶךְ שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.2\">1 K 21:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 1:3\" href=\"/II_Kings.1.3\">2 K 1:3</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ יִשׂ׳ אֲשֶׁר בְּשׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 21:18\" href=\"/I_Kings.21.18\">1 K 21:18</a>, cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מָלַךְ עַל־יִשׂ׳ בְּשׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:52\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.52\">22:52</a> + 9 times; thence name of territory, <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׂדֵה שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Obadiah 1:19\" href=\"/Obadiah.1.19\">Ob 19</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עָרֵי שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 13:32\" href=\"/I_Kings.13.32\">1 K 13:32</a> (point of view of later editor), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:24\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.24\">2 K 17:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:26\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.26\">26</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:19\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.19\">23:19</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרֵי שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 3:9\" href=\"/Amos.3.9\">Am 3:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.5\">Je 31:5</a>,—cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 4:1\" href=\"/Amos.4.1\">Am 4:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Amos 6:1\" href=\"/Amos.6.1\">6:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:24\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.24\">1 K 16:24</a>; perhaps <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ׳</span> alone <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 23:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.23.13\">Je 23:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.2\">1 K 18:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:24\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.24\">2 K 17:24</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Kings 17:28\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.28\">28</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 25:13\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.25.13\">2 Ch 25:13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵיל שׁ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 3:34\" href=\"/Nehemiah.3.34\">Ne 3:34</a>.—𝔊 usually Σαμαρεια, but <a data-ref=\"I Kings 16:24\" href=\"/I_Kings.16.24\">1 K 16:24</a> Σεμερω, Σαεμερων, Σομορων; = mod. <em>Sebastieh;</em> vid. GASm<sup>G. 346 ff.</sup> Buhl <sup>G 207 f.</sup> Cowley<sup>Ency. Bib. s. v.</sup> Wilson<sup>Hast. DB s. v.</sup>.","next":"BDB, שֹׁמְרֹנִי","prev":"BDB, שְׁמַרְיָ֫ה(וּ)"}